<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<% content_for :meta, social_meta(description: "Why Midrolo exists, where its data comes from, and what it is built on: Qloo taste data, each show's own feed, verified Spotify and Apple numbers and an AI model.") %>
<div class="wrap page-head">
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1 class="type-h1">About <%= APP_NAME %></h1>
    <p class="type-lead">
      <%= APP_NAME %> is where independent podcasts get sponsored: brands find shows their customers love, and podcasters
      list their show free. The name comes from the midroll, the ad slot that pays best in an episode.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Small shows want sponsors but can't show brands who their listeners are: hosting stats count downloads and countries,
      not taste. Brands can't find small shows that fit, rates are rarely published, and the numbers can't be checked.
      The tools that could help are priced for agencies, and the marketplaces built for small shows keep closing.
      <%= APP_NAME %> gives both sides the evidence: taste matching from Qloo, sponsor history from each show's own feed,
      and numbers verified at the source.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Qloo</strong>'s taste graph: what people with your listeners' tastes love more than most people do, how they lean by age and gender, and where they live.</li>
      <li><strong>Podcast Index</strong>: podcast search and show details. Podcast data from <a class="link" href="https://podcastindex.org">Podcast Index</a>, the open podcast directory.</li>
      <li><strong>Public RSS feeds</strong>: each show's page, its episodes, and the sponsor reads in its episode notes.</li>
      <li><strong>Spotify for Creators and Apple Podcasts Connect</strong>: a show's verified numbers, read with our own account once the show invites <%= APP_NAME %>.</li>
      <li><strong>AI models</strong>, through OpenRouter: plan the research, check sponsor reads, and write the reasons, pitches and briefs from those results.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Audiences are modeled from Qloo taste data, not measured, and every report says so. Every number on a show's page says where it came from and when.</p>

    <h2>Where it's at</h2>
    <p>
      <%= APP_NAME %> was built for the Qloo Agentic Hackathon in October 2026.
      <% if Billing.mode == :live %>
        Paid plans are open.
      <% else %>
        Paid plans aren't on sale yet: billing is built and tested in test mode, and you can join the founding member
        waitlist from the <%= link_to "pricing page", pricing_path, class: "link" %>.
      <% end %>
      Its code is open source under the AGPL-3.0 license.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, feedback or a show we got wrong: <%= contact_mail_to class: "link" %>.</p>
  </article>
</div>
